<title>USA: Rare Hospitality chief executive to leave.</title>
<headline>Rare Hospitality chief executive to leave.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>RARE Hospitality International Inc on Monday said its chief executive and president, Richard Rivera, would resign August 29 to pursue other interests.</p>
<p>Chairman George McKerrow will become acting president and chief executive until a permanent replacement is found, the company said, adding that its board has appointed a committee to search for a successor.</p>
<p>The company, formally called Longhorn Steaks, operates and franchises 109 restaurants.</p>
</text>
